  "worked_solution": "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z=f(x,y)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ on the surface can be written as\n\n$$\nz-{z}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{\u2202f}{\u2202x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{\u2202f}{\u2202y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}).\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\u2202f}{\u2202x} & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061({x}^{2}y)-{y}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{({x}^{2}y)^{2}+1}\\cdot 2xy \\\\  & =\\frac{2xy}{{x}^{4}{y}^{2}+1} \\\\ \\frac{\u2202f}{\u2202y} & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061({x}^{2}y)-{y}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{({x}^{2}y)^{2}+1}\\cdot {x}^{2}-3{y}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{4}{y}^{2}+1}-3{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNext, we evaluate the partial derivatives at $(x,y)=(2,0):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\u2202f}{\u2202x}(2,0) & =\\frac{2(2)(0)}{(2)^{4}(0)^{2}+1}=0 \\\\ \\frac{\u2202f}{\u2202y}(2,0) & =\\frac{(2)^{2}}{(2)^{4}(0)^{2}+1}-3(0)^{2}=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we write down the equation of the tangent plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-0 & =(x-0)\\frac{\u2202f}{\u2202x}(2,0)+(y-0)\\frac{\u2202f}{\u2202y}(2,0) \\\\ z & =0(x-0)+4(y-0) \\\\ z & =4y \\\\ 4y-z & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$",
